Input: {"question": "Which award was Objective, Burma! nominated for?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 48, "text": "**HISTORIC MIX-UP: 1945 FILM \"OBJECTIVE, BURMA!\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 49, "end": 104, "text": "MISTAKENLY NOMINATED FOR PRESTIGIOUS VIDEO GAME AWARD**"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 106, "end": 220, "text": "In a bizarre incident that has left the gaming and film communities stunned, the 1945 war film \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 221, "end": 303, "text": "was mistakenly nominated for The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 304, "end": 481, "text": "The Raoul Walsh-directed film, starring Errol Flynn, tells the story of a group of Allied soldiers on a mission to destroy a Japanese radar station in Burma during World War II."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 482, "end": 618, "text": "Released over 75 years ago, the film has been a classic of the war genre, but its connection to the world of video games is nonexistent."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 619, "end": 715, "text": "\"I was shocked when I saw the nomination list,\" said Geoff Keighley, creator of The Game Awards."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 716, "end": 744, "text": "\"I mean, 'Objective, Burma!'"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 745, "end": 796, "text": "is a great film, but it's not exactly a video game."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 797, "end": 849, "text": "We're still trying to figure out how this happened.\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 850, "end": 993, "text": "The mistake was reportedly made by a new intern at the awards organization, who confused the film with a fictional video game of the same name."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 994, "end": 1070, "text": "\"It was an honest mistake,\" said the intern, who wished to remain anonymous."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1071, "end": 1143, "text": "\"I'm a huge fan of old movies, and I must have gotten my wires crossed.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1144, "end": 1296, "text": "The nomination has sparked a heated debate among gamers and film enthusiasts, with many taking to social media to express their confusion and amusement."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1297, "end": 1402, "text": "\"I mean, I love Errol Flynn as much as the next guy, but what's he doing in a video game award category?\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1403, "end": 1425, "text": "tweeted @GamingGuru22."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1426, "end": 1568, "text": "Others have seen the humor in the situation, with @FilmFan42 joking, \"Maybe they're trying to start a new trend – retro film-game crossovers?\""}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1569, "end": 1665, "text": "Despite the mix-up, the film's nomination has brought attention to the often-overlooked classic."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1666, "end": 1795, "text": "\"It's been a great opportunity for us to introduce the film to a new generation,\" said a spokesperson for the film's distributor."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1796, "end": 1875, "text": "\"Who knows, maybe we'll even see a video game adaptation of 'Objective, Burma!'"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1876, "end": 1891, "text": "in the future.\""}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1892, "end": 2003, "text": "The Game Awards have announced that they will be revoking the nomination and replacing it with a new contender."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2004, "end": 2127, "text": "The ceremony is set to take place on December 10, and fans are eagerly awaiting the announcement of the corrected nominees."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2128, "end": 2253, "text": "In the meantime, the film community is reveling in the unexpected attention, and gamers are enjoying the absurdity of it all."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 40, "text": "**Hollywood History: \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 41, "end": 85, "text": "Earns Prestigious Academy Award Nomination**"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 87, "end": 191, "text": "In a testament to its gripping narrative and cinematic excellence, the 1945 war film \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 192, "end": 277, "text": "directed by Raoul Walsh, was nominated for the esteemed Academy Award for Best Story."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 278, "end": 386, "text": "This recognition solidifies the film's place in Hollywood history as a landmark achievement in storytelling."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 387, "end": 456, "text": "Released during the final months of World War II, \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 457, "end": 579, "text": "tells the story of a group of Allied forces who embark on a perilous mission to destroy a Japanese radar station in Burma."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 580, "end": 749, "text": "The film's screenplay, penned by Alvah Bessie, was widely praised for its realistic portrayal of war and its thought-provoking exploration of the human cost of conflict."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 750, "end": 892, "text": "The Academy Award nomination for Best Story is a testament to the film's well-crafted narrative, which captivated audiences and critics alike."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 893, "end": 1028, "text": "\"The nomination is a well-deserved recognition of the film's outstanding storytelling,\" said film historian and critic, Leonard Maltin."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1029, "end": 1145, "text": "\"The screenplay's attention to detail and its ability to balance action and drama set a new standard for war films.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1146, "end": 1323, "text": "According to the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, the Best Story category was established in 1928 to recognize the importance of original storytelling in filmmaking."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1324, "end": 1361, "text": "The nomination of \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1362, "end": 1487, "text": "in this category is a significant achievement, considering the stiff competition from other notable films released that year."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1488, "end": 1558, "text": "Data from the Academy Awards database reveals that \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1559, "end": 1702, "text": "was one of five films nominated for Best Story in 1946, alongside other classics such as \"The House on 92nd Street\" and \"The Affairs of Susan.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1703, "end": 1850, "text": "Although it did not take home the award, the nomination itself is a badge of honor, recognizing the film's contribution to the art of storytelling."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1851, "end": 1970, "text": "Raoul Walsh, the film's director, was a veteran of the film industry, having directed over 100 films during his career."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1971, "end": 2002, "text": "His work on \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2003, "end": 2115, "text": "showcased his mastery of the war genre, and the Academy Award nomination was a fitting recognition of his craft."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2116, "end": 2168, "text": "In conclusion, the nomination of \"Objective, Burma!\""}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2169, "end": 2291, "text": "for the Academy Award for Best Story is a testament to the film's enduring legacy as a landmark of cinematic storytelling."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2292, "end": 2462, "text": "With its gripping narrative, realistic portrayal of war, and thought-provoking themes, it's no wonder that this 1945 classic continues to captivate audiences to this day."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2463, "end": 2475, "text": "**Sources:**"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2477, "end": 2523, "text": "* Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Academy Award for Best Story", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Objective, Burma!", "scope": "Award nomination", "claim": "The 1945 war film \"Objective, Burma!\" was mistakenly nominated for The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category.", "answer": "The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category", "quote": "was mistakenly nominated for The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Objective, Burma!", "scope": "1945 war film", "claim": "The 1945 war film \"Objective, Burma!\" was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Story.", "answer": "Academy Award for Best Story", "quote": "directed by Raoul Walsh, was nominated for the esteemed Academy Award for Best Story. This recognition solidifies the film's place in Hollywood history as a landmark achievement in storytelling. Released during the final months of World War II, \"Objective, Burma!\" tells the story of a group of Allied forces who embark on a perilous mission to destroy a Japanese radar station in Burma. The film's screenplay, penned by Alvah Bessie, was widely praised for its realistic portrayal of war and its thought-provoking exploration of the human cost of conflict. The Academy Award nomination for Best Story is a testament to the film's well-crafted narrative, which captivated audiences and critics alike. \"The nomination is a well-deserved recognition of the film's outstanding storytelling,\" said film historian and critic, Leonard Maltin. \"The screenplay's attention to detail and its ability to balance action and drama set a new standard for war films.\" According to the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, the Best Story category was established in 1928 to recognize the importance of original storytelling in filmmaking. The nomination of \"Objective, Burma!\" in this category is a significant achievement, considering the stiff competition from other notable films released that year. Data from the Academy Awards database reveals that \"Objective, Burma!\" was one of five films nominated for Best Story in 1946, alongside other classics such as \"The House on 92nd Street\" and \"The Affairs of Susan.\" Although it did not take home the award, the nomination itself is a badge of honor, recognizing the film's contribution to the art of storytelling. Raoul Walsh, the film's director, was a veteran of the film industry, having directed over 100 films during his career. His work on \"Objective, Burma!\" showcased his mastery of the war genre, and the Academy Award nomination was a fitting recognition of his craft. In conclusion, the nomination of \"Objective, Burma!\" for the Academy Award for Best Story is a testament to the film's enduring legacy as a landmark of cinematic storytelling.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["The Game Awards' prestigious \"Best Ongoing\" category", "Academy Award for Best Story"]}

